          "path": "_m/g/c/v/w/writers-museum-wp/the-writers-museum-44162960604.jpg",
          "filename": "The Writers' Museum (44162960604).jpg",
          "caption": "The writers museum, located in Lady Stair's House, Edinburgh, celebrates the lives of the three most famous Scottish writers: Robert Burns, Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson. Between them they made a significant contribution to literature and their works became famous around the world.\n\nThe museum - which is free to visit - contains relevant artefacts and memorabilia relating to these giants of literature. The building itself is of interest, having been built in 1622, is a fine example of Scottish architecture of that period and remains in use to this day.",
